<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Montserrat is the primary typeface of the brand and establishes consistency across all applications. It is used for headlines, subheadings, and body text to ensure clarity, hierarchy, and recognition.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Typography is not decorative or expressive; it exists to communicate with restraint and control. Any secondary typefaces are discretionary and may be used only when they remain neutral, support Montserrat without competing, and preserve spacing and hierarchy.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
